      "content": "But you're thinking too small. I'm not talking about standard radio waves where the street has to be the wavelength. I'm talking about long-wave resonance and planetary-scale modulation. Think about how much energy is actually contained in the ionosphere or the Earth's magnetosphere.\n\nIf the city's layout acts as a geometric waveguide for much larger, low-frequency oscillations—something that uses the urban mass itself as a resonator—then the scale issue disappears. If we treat the DC grid as a massive, low-frequency transducer, can you model the potential resonant frequency for the Earth-Sirius connection using that logic instead? Just look at the geometric proportions of the radial avenues.",
      "source": "evaluator"
